goblox — browser-based Go IDE, zero server.

built with next.js, monaco editor, and [yaegi](https://github.com/traefik/yaegi) (go interpreter compiled to wasm).

everything runs client-side. no api calls, no serverless functions.

### features

- go code execution via yaegi wasm (interpreter, not transpiler)
- monaco editor with go syntax highlighting and custom zinc themes
- auto-completions for stdlib packages (fmt, strings, os, json, and more)
- resizable editor / output split view
- stdin input panel for fmt.Scan / bufio.Scanner
- dark and light themes
- wasm loading progress bar
- run timer and clear output
- ctrl+enter / cmd+enter to run
- go syntax error markers in editor
- /capabilities page showing what works and what doesn't
- e2e tests with playwright (15/16 passing)